---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import {
  discordUrl,
  routes,
  withBasePath
} from '../config/site';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const privacyUrl = withBasePath(base, routes.privacy);
const contactEmail = 'Elliott@ElPlugins.com';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service - ElPlugins"
  description="ElPlugins Terms of Service."
>
  <Navbar />

  <main>
    <section class="page-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p>
        Effective 7 July 2026. Last reviewed 7 July 2026. These terms apply to
        ElPlugins, the launcher, plugins, Discord support, purchases and related
        services.
      </p>

      <div class="page-actions">
        <a class="button discord-button" href={discordUrl}>Contact Us on Discord</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="tos-page">
      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>Agreement to Our Legal Terms</h2>

        <p>
          We are ElPlugins, a trading name also referred to as "we", "us" or
          "our". We operate the ElPlugins website, Discord server, launcher,
          plugins, support channels, store listings and related services that
          refer or link to these terms.
        </p>

        <p>
          You can contact us through the Discord ticket system or by email at
          {' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>. Discord tickets
          are the official support channel and the starting point for informal
          dispute notices.
        </p>

        <p>
          These terms form a legally binding agreement between you and
          ElPlugins. By accessing, buying or using the services, you confirm
          that you have read, understood and agreed to these terms.
        </p>

        <p>
          If you do not agree to these terms, you must not purchase, access or
          use the services.
        </p>

        <p>
          The services are intended for users who are at least 13 years old.
          Minors must have permission from, and be supervised by, a parent or
          guardian.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>1. Our Services</h2>

        <p>
          ElPlugins provides plugin access, launcher access, Discord support and
          related digital services. The services may depend on third-party
          platforms, game clients, operating systems, payment processors,
          hosting providers and Discord.
        </p>

        <p>
          You are responsible for making sure your use of the services is lawful
          in your location and consistent with any third-party rules that apply
          to you.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>2. Intellectual Property Rights</h2>

        <p>
          We own or license the intellectual property rights in the services,
          including source code, software, launcher functionality, plugins,
          website content, text, graphics, logos, designs, documentation and
          related materials.
        </p>

        <p>
          Subject to your compliance with these terms, we grant you a limited,
          personal, revocable, non-exclusive and non-transferable licence to
          access and use the services you have properly purchased or otherwise
          been granted access to.
        </p>

        <p>
          You must not copy, sell, rent, share, sublicense, publish, distribute,
          decompile, reverse engineer, modify, bypass protection for, or exploit
          any part of the services except where we have expressly allowed it in
          writing or applicable law prevents us from restricting it.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>3. User Accounts and Representations</h2>

        <p>By using the services, you represent and agree that:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>Your registration, Discord, purchase and support information is accurate and kept up to date.</li>
          <li>You have legal capacity to agree to these terms.</li>
          <li>You are at least 13 years old, and if you are a minor you have parent or guardian permission.</li>
          <li>You will keep account, launcher, key and access information secure.</li>
          <li>You will not use automated or non-human access methods unless we expressly allow them.</li>
          <li>You will not use the services for illegal, abusive or unauthorised purposes.</li>
          <li>Your use of the services will not violate applicable law or regulation.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          If information you provide is false, inaccurate, incomplete or
          misleading, we may suspend, restrict or terminate access.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>4. Purchases, Payments and Delivery</h2>

        <p>
          We may accept payment through Stripe-supported methods, store checkout
          methods, cryptocurrency and manually verified in-game currency such as
          Old School RuneScape Gold Pieces. Available payment methods may change
          at any time.
        </p>

        <p>
          You must provide current, complete and accurate purchase information.
          Prices, packages, availability and accepted currencies may change at
          any time. Taxes, fees or currency conversion costs may apply depending
          on your payment method and location.
        </p>

        <p>
          A purchase is treated as delivered when the relevant Discord role,
          launcher access, key, subscription, plugin access or other access
          entitlement has been provided.
        </p>

        <p>
          Subscriptions and package access are fixed-term access periods unless
          we clearly state otherwise. They do not automatically renew. You are
          responsible for renewing access manually before or after expiry.
        </p>

        <p>
          Sales are final once access has been delivered. Refunds are not
          provided except where required by law, where a duplicate charge is
          confirmed, or where a proven payment processing error occurred.
        </p>

        <p>
          Cryptocurrency payments are processed after sufficient network
          confirmation. Cryptocurrency values and fees may fluctuate, and we do
          not promise cryptocurrency refunds. In-game currency payments are
          manually verified and are final once accepted. You are responsible for
          any risk connected with using in-game currency, including third-party
          game rules or enforcement.
        </p>

        <p>
          We may refuse, cancel, correct or limit any order where there is a
          pricing error, stock or access issue, suspected fraud, abuse, payment
          dispute, technical problem or breach of these terms.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>5. Software Licence and HWID Rules</h2>

        <p>
          The launcher, plugins and related software are licensed, not sold. You
          receive a personal, limited, revocable, non-transferable licence to use
          them only for your own access during the relevant active access period.
        </p>

        <p>
          You must not share, resell, rent, leak, transfer or make available any
          key, plugin, launcher file, account access, Discord role, media,
          configuration or other access entitlement. Access is linked to your
          Discord account and may also be linked to hardware identifiers.
        </p>

        <p>
          One HWID means one device, including a PC, laptop or server. Activating
          a plugin binds it to that device for 30 days, and each later use resets
          the 30-day timer. You may run unlimited plugin instances on an allowed
          HWID, but plugins remain for personal use only.
        </p>

        <p>
          To remove a HWID, you must either wait 30 days without activating the
          plugin or pay a $5 reset fee, payable in accepted in-game currency or
          cryptocurrency, for an immediate reset. HWIDs are linked to your
          Discord account. Creating a new account may avoid a reset fee, but it
          does not allow you to avoid enforcement, payment or abuse checks.
        </p>

        <p>
          Hardware changes, including CPU or motherboard changes, can change
          your HWID. If that happens, you must wait 30 days or pay the $5 reset
          fee before using the plugin on the changed HWID.
        </p>

        <p>Unless a product page or support notice says otherwise, HWID limits are:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>Package access for 30, 60, 90 days or lifetime: 2 HWIDs.</li>
          <li>PVM access for 30, 60, 90 days or lifetime: 1 HWID.</li>
          <li>Package and PVM combined access for 30, 60 or 90 days: 1 HWID.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Updates may be required to continue using the services. We do not
          guarantee compatibility with every game version, game client, launcher,
          operating system, device, hardware setup, third-party service or future
          update.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>6. Prohibited Activities</h2>

        <p>You agree not to:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>Share, sell, transfer, leak or resell keys, plugins, subscriptions, files, Discord access or launcher access.</li>
          <li>Copy, adapt, decompile, disassemble, decipher, bypass, tamper with or reverse engineer software or protection systems.</li>
          <li>Use bots, scripts, scrapers, automated tools or data extraction tools against the services unless approved.</li>
          <li>Interfere with security features, access controls, payment checks, HWID checks or abuse-prevention systems.</li>
          <li>Submit false, misleading, abusive or bad-faith reports, disputes, support requests or payment claims.</li>
          <li>Open chargebacks or payment disputes without first trying to resolve the issue through Discord ticket support.</li>
          <li>Advertise personal services, competing services or unauthorised commercial activity through our platform.</li>
          <li>Affiliate with cracking, hacking, leaking, account-sharing, key-sharing or similar communities or services.</li>
          <li>Harass, threaten, abuse, impersonate or mislead staff, customers or other users.</li>
          <li>Upload malware, spam, disruptive content or material that creates an undue burden on the services.</li>
          <li>Use the services in a way that violates law, regulation, third-party rights or these terms.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Depending on the severity, evidence and risk, we may warn, suspend,
          restrict, revoke or terminate access. Serious or repeated breaches may
          result in immediate removal without refund.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>7. Contributions and Reviews</h2>

        <p>
          The services may let you submit messages, reviews, feedback, support
          content, screenshots, suggestions or other materials. You remain
          responsible for what you submit and must have the rights needed to
          submit it.
        </p>

        <p>
          You grant us a limited, non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free licence
          to host, store, display, reproduce, moderate, edit, remove and use your
          contributions only as reasonably needed to operate, provide, protect,
          support and improve the services.
        </p>

        <p>
          We do not claim ownership of your contributions. We may remove or
          moderate contributions at any time, especially where they are false,
          abusive, illegal, misleading, discriminatory, threatening, obscene,
          spam, infringing or otherwise unsuitable.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>8. Privacy</h2>

        <p>
          We handle personal information according to our
          {' '}
          <a href={privacyUrl}>Privacy Policy</a>. The Privacy Policy explains
          what information we collect, how we use it, which third-party services
          may process it, and how privacy requests can be made.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>9. Support, Availability and Maintenance</h2>

        <p>
          Support is provided through Discord tickets on a reasonable-efforts
          basis. We do not guarantee any specific response time, resolution time
          or outcome.
        </p>

        <p>
          The services may be unavailable, interrupted, delayed, limited or
          changed because of maintenance, updates, outages, third-party services,
          security work, payment issues, compatibility changes or operational
          reasons.
        </p>

        <p>
          We do not guarantee uptime or continuous compatibility. We may, at our
          discretion, offer extensions or credits for significant downtime, but
          these are not automatic and are not guaranteed.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>10. Termination</h2>

        <p>
          These terms apply while you access or use the services. We may suspend,
          restrict, revoke or terminate your access if you breach these terms,
          create risk for ElPlugins or other users, abuse payment or support
          processes, or where we need to protect the services.
        </p>

        <p>
          Termination does not remove obligations that should reasonably survive,
          including payment obligations, licence restrictions, intellectual
          property protections, disclaimers, liability limits and dispute terms.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>11. Changes and Corrections</h2>

        <p>
          We may update services, packages, prices, features, compatibility
          details and these terms from time to time. We may correct errors,
          inaccuracies or omissions, including descriptions, pricing,
          availability and access information.
        </p>

        <p>
          Updated terms take effect when posted unless we state a later date.
          Continuing to use the services after changes are posted means you
          accept the updated terms.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>12. Disclaimers</h2>

        <p>
          The services are provided on an as-is and as-available basis. To the
          fullest extent permitted by law, we disclaim warranties and conditions
          of any kind, whether express, implied or statutory, including implied
          warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose,
          non-infringement and uninterrupted availability.
        </p>

        <p>
          You are responsible for your own use of the services, your device,
          accounts, third-party platform obligations and any third-party
          consequences connected with your use.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>13. Limitation of Liability</h2>

        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, ElPlugins will not be liable
          for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary or punitive
          losses, or for loss of profit, revenue, data, goodwill, access,
          opportunity or business.
        </p>

        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, our total liability for any
          claim connected with the services is limited to the amount you paid to
          ElPlugins for the affected service in the 30 days before the claim
          arose.
        </p>

        <p>
          Nothing in these terms limits liability where it would be unlawful to
          do so.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>14. Disputes, Governing Law and Courts</h2>

        <p>
          Before starting formal proceedings, you and ElPlugins agree to try to
          resolve disputes informally for at least 30 days through the Discord
          ticket system, unless urgent legal action is required.
        </p>

        <p>
          These terms and any dispute or claim connected with them, their subject
          matter or formation are governed by the laws of England and Wales.
        </p>

        <p>
          The courts of England and Wales will have exclusive jurisdiction over
          disputes connected with these terms or the services, except where
          applicable consumer law gives you mandatory rights in another court.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>15. Miscellaneous</h2>

        <p>
          These terms, together with any policies or product rules we post,
          represent the agreement between you and ElPlugins for the services.
          Our failure to enforce a term does not waive our right to enforce it
          later.
        </p>

        <p>
          If any part of these terms is found invalid or unenforceable, the rest
          remains in effect. You may not transfer your rights or obligations
          under these terms without our written permission.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="tos-card">
        <h2>16. Contact Us</h2>

        <p>
          For support or complaints, open a Discord ticket:
          {' '}
          <a href={discordUrl}>{discordUrl}</a>.
        </p>

        <p>
          For legal or contact purposes, email
          {' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
        </p>

        <p>ElPlugins</p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />

  <style>
    .tos-page {
      padding: 70px 6vw 90px;
      display: grid;
      gap: 20px;
      max-width: 1160px;
    }

    .tos-card {
      padding: 30px;
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at top right, rgba(255, 216, 74, 0.09), transparent 18rem),
        linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(36, 31, 19, 0.88), rgba(16, 14, 9, 0.95));
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }

    .tos-card h2 {
      margin-top: 0;
      font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 2.4vw, 2.1rem);
    }

    .tos-card p,
    .tos-card li {
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.72;
    }

    .tos-card a {
      color: var(--gold-bright);
      font-weight: 900;
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 4px;
    }

    .tos-card ul {
      margin: 16px 0 0;
      padding-left: 20px;
    }

    @media (max-width: 760px) {
      .tos-page {
        padding-left: 22px;
        padding-right: 22px;
      }

      .tos-card {
        padding: 24px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
